{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "To thee, traveler of the land of rising sun, I present a journey through Japan, with a quill dipped in the ink of Shakespearean verse, without the commas to mar the flow.\n\nDay one, set sail for Tokyo, the heart of Japan, there to behold the majesty of the Shard, the Tokyo Skytree, a spire reaching to the heavens. And in the evening, stroll through the neon-lit streets of Shinjuku, where the bustling life of the city doth come alive, and in the shadow of the tower, a play of light and form, a dance of neon and night.\n\nOn the second day, venture to Kyoto, the city of a thousand temples, where the ancient and the modern doth coexist. Walk through the gates of Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion, where the reflection of the pavilion in the pond doth mirror the beauty of nature, and in the garden, the path of the Zen garden, a journey of the soul.\n\nDay three, immerse in the tranquility of nature at Arashiyama, where the bamboo groves stand tall and proud, and the Togetsukyo Bridge doth span the Katsura River. And in the Hozu River, a journey by boat, where the scenery doth unfold like a scroll of art.\n\nFourth day, journey to Nara, the ancient capital, where deer roam freely, and the Todai-ji doth stand as a testament to the grandeur of the past. In the Daibutsu, a statue of Buddha, a symbol of peace and enlightenment.\n\nFifth day, return to Tokyo, and in the morning, visit the Tsukiji Outer Market, where the bounty of the sea doth await, and savor the sushi crafted by master chefs, a taste of the ocean in each bite.\n\nLastly, on the sixth day, take leave of Tokyo, with memories of the journey etched in the heart, and a wish to return to this land of beauty and wonder, where the past and present doth dance in harmony.", "logprobs": [{"token": "To", "logprob": -2.2240729331970215}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.537112832069397}, {"token": "e